    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d612">

                <pb facs="0835" n="733" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg733"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">765.84/743: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Ethiopia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Engert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Addis Ababa</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-08-05T18:00:00+02:35">August 5, 1935—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received August 5—2:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>69. At an audience I had this afternoon with the Emperor he expressed gratitude
                    for the statement made by the President on August 1st which he considers typical
                    of the love of peace of the American people. His Majesty also referred in kindly
                    terms to the helpful work of the American missionaries in Ethiopia.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Engert</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
